    "prerequisite_note": "Use test-design preconditions and controlled-fixture concepts before minimizing a reproduction.",
    "practice": "What does a minimal reproduction preserve?|The relevant failure|Only the final click|Every original log line|The suspected fix|Minimization removes irrelevant detail while retaining the behavior and its meaningful conditions.|The trigger may depend on history;All logs may not be necessary;A fix is not a failing reproduction.\nWhy record initial state?|Interpret the action|Guarantee all environments agree|Avoid expected results|Prove the root cause|The same action can have different correct results under different starting conditions.|A record does not force parity;An oracle is still needed;State alone does not establish cause.\nA failure happens once in ten runs. How should it be described?|Intermittent with evidence|Unconditionally reproducible|Certainly not a defect|Guaranteed random noise|Observed frequency and conditions should be reported without overstating certainty.|Not every run reproduced it;Intermittence does not negate harm;Noise is a causal claim requiring evidence.\nRemoving a cancellation step stops the failure. What may that show?|History is relevant|The issue was fabricated|All cancellations are unsafe|The final click is irrelevant|The removed step may establish state needed for the observed failure.|A smaller passing case does not erase the original;One sequence does not prove every cancellation;The final action may still participate.\nA random fixture failure has only a seed saved. What else can matter?|Inputs and tool context|Only ticket color|Only author seniority|Only file naming|Reproduction may depend on generated data, versions and nonrandom external state.|Display metadata does not recreate conditions;Seniority is not execution context;Names alone do not supply data.\nA local sequence model passes. What should not be claimed?|Real race disproven|That the model ran|That its output matched|That inputs were synthetic|Sequential local behavior does not establish concurrent production behavior.|Execution is directly observed;Output comparison is scoped evidence;Synthetic inputs can be declared.",
    "formal": "What is minimization for?|Reduce irrelevant detail|Erase the triggering state|Guarantee a known cause|Change the requirement|A smaller reproducer helps diagnosis while preserving the original failure mechanism and oracle.|Removing the trigger loses the case;Simplicity does not prove cause;The rule should not be altered to keep a symptom.\nWhich record helps identify tested software?|Immutable artifact identity|Only a mutable latest label|Only staff job title|Only issue age|An immutable identifier ties reproduction evidence to a particular artifact.|Mutable labels can move;A role does not identify bytes;Age is not build identity.\nWhy distinguish consistent and intermittent behavior?|Report repeatability|Decide blame automatically|Remove all uncertainty|Replace environment details|The report should preserve how reliably the observed conditions reproduce the discrepancy.|Frequency does not identify a person at fault;Intermittence retains uncertainty;Context is still necessary.\nAn LMS retry fails only after cancellation. What must a useful reproduction retain?|The state-changing sequence|Only the last page reload|Only a fresh success account|Only the final error text|Earlier actions may create the state needed for the retry failure.|A reload can omit the trigger;A fresh account may not reproduce history;An error text lacks preconditions.\nA retailer deletes half the fixture and sees a different error. What should be checked?|Failure equivalence|Only attachment size|Only report title length|Only assigned priority|Minimization must retain the same meaningful discrepancy rather than substitute a new failure.|Size alone does not show relevance;Titles do not establish behavior;Priority does not compare mechanisms.\nA bank\u2019s timeout issue occurs under an external outage. How should the condition be recorded?|Explicit dependency state|As a universal failure|As a proven local-only bug|Instead of the expected result|The dependency condition is part of the evidence scope and can affect the correct outcome.|One outage does not imply all conditions;Local cause is unproven;An oracle remains required.\nA hospital cannot safely recreate a live failure. What is responsible?|Use bounded isolated evidence|Copy all patient data blindly|Declare it nonexistent|Trigger the live action repeatedly|Safe synthetic reproduction and retained observations can support investigation without live harm.|Unrestricted data copying violates minimization;Lack of replay does not erase observation;Repeated real effects can cause damage.\nA logistics seed replays different inputs after a generator upgrade. What does this show?|Version-sensitive reproduction|A guaranteed fake report|A fixed seed never matters|All random testing is useless|Seeds support replay only with relevant generator behavior and surrounding context.|A version change can explain differences;Seeds still provide useful information;Random exploration can be valuable.\nA SaaS test reproduces a timing failure only with an artificial delay. What should be clear?|The scheduling assumption|That production cause is proven|That every request fails|That delay is the correct fix|The delay supplies controlled evidence about one schedule without proving all live causes.|A model is not a causal guarantee;One schedule does not cover every request;A reproducer is not necessarily a remedy.\nA university issue stops reproducing after a configuration change. What should the update state?|Conditions and observed result|It never happened|The original evidence is false|All configurations are safe|A changed condition can alter behavior while the original observation remains valid within its scope.|Later success cannot rewrite history;Different conditions do not invalidate past evidence;Other configurations remain untested."
